{
 "_about": "Emerald General (leob0505's ORAS set, data/tilesets/primary/leob_general) + the Brick City kit (data/tilesets/secondary/brick_city; Ekat99, imported by Kumatora; see its CREDITS.md). Saltwick, the Holding Meadow and Route 1. 'c' is the kit's flagstone paving, 'p'/'s' General's sand track; the paths pass gives every cell its edges. T is the Skaldmere fir (2x2; palette 12, which the kit leaves free and brick_city.py fills), N the small spruce as a wood (palette 2: the only tree allowed within eight rows of the Mistwood seam, whose kit has its own palette 12). Quay: 'n' wall to the north of the water, '>' to the east, '<' to the west, 'e'/'q' the two inside corners, 'u'/'v' the outside ones (887-891 are brick_city.py's additions). '{' and '}' are General's rock bank on a water cell, land to the west and to the east: the wooded banks that close the harbour, so the border's firs never stand in open water. ':' is the kit's road; paving beside it gets a kerb. 'i' a lamp on paving, '=' a bench, '&' and '%' hedge planters, 'O' the fountain, G/E/I/C the gabled houses, W the hall with its steps '( _ )'. '-' '^' '|' ''' are the water cells on either side of a bridge (its north edge, the arches and their piers, the shadow), '+' a plank jetty over the sea, 'w' a plank footbridge, '$' ';' the two cells of a stair across a ledge.",
